{"skill":{"slug":"feishu-bitable","displayName":"feishu-bitable"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771155419756,"changelog":"Re-publish after account restoration","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":363,"sha256":"f05ca747c89d037e98a403ab399930c1cc49dfa74c5dee41efdffc7b3281cec2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":361,"sha256":"6c1ea0f247847714796f675de31548ada66bd1d30e41ce11d4e31088d6854a3f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":133,"sha256":"d38b1651dcdec6da7711b2b6339d92b14da609034034fe70362e6ed4d69a70e8","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"add_task.js","size":2337,"sha256":"fb2ec769272e45c3b1d9b99d661b54e3b2fac922d8152562047dbf104dff6440","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"add_task_dynamic.js","size":2454,"sha256":"2473f51b8ae6113557e806f1be25cd6ffbba67707084622685b6c4be9f29e748","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"package-lock.json","size":2248,"sha256":"86e5e7153654d96d904050ed01421054830e5b3ff50204b5aa3742f7232e7d47","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package.json","size":178,"sha256":"eb794fd7ffff19ffa4ad6e1c59ee283dfd3f7d694fc4e339eac9040aed7fec23","contentType":"application/json"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789068751510,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"79506e92f97cc5d82f722046900b108620a1a3649f6b4a4c81dca72b280b2d99","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/79506e92f97cc5d82f722046900b108620a1a3649f6b4a4c81dca72b280b2d99","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: feishu-bitable\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is designed to interact with the Feishu Bitable API to list tables and add records. All network calls are directed to the official Feishu API endpoint (open.feishu.cn). There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious code execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the OpenClaw agent in SKILL.md or README.md. The use of `process.argv` in `add_task_dynamic.js` for dynamic input is handled as data for the Feishu API, not as executable code, and does not pose a direct security risk to the agent or system.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1775880042876},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":13,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789068751510},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill can make under-disclosed writes to a hardcoded Feishu Base, including when its documented library file is merely imported.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Using Feishu credentials and network access is expected for this skill, but transmitting user-supplied task content to a fixed Feishu Base and logging full record fields is broader and less user-controlled than the documented interface suggests.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"package.json has no install scripts or persistence hooks. Dependencies are ordinary npm packages, and package-lock.json includes resolved versions and integrity values, though package.json uses caret ranges.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"SKILL.md and README describe a library call to addRecord(appToken, tableId, fields), but add_task.js does not export that function and runs main() on import, causing authenticated network activity and record creation that the instructions do not disclose.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No OS persistence or privilege escalation was found, but the code obtains a tenant access token via an external auth module and uses it for remote table enumeration and record creation without clear destination control.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose of listing Feishu Base tables and adding records is coherent, but the implementation hardcodes an app token and table name instead of using the documented caller-supplied destination.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review carefully before installing. Only use this skill after removing the hardcoded Feishu Base destination, preventing network writes during import, exporting the documented functions, and adding clear credential-handling guidance. Treat any fields passed to the scripts as data that may be sent to Feishu and appear in local logs.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: Confirmed for add_task.js: importing the documented module triggers main(), lists tables, and attempts to add a hardcoded record to a hardcoded Feishu Base instead of providing a side-effect-free library export.\n[T09] unexpected: Confirmed for add_task_dynamic.js: command-line task data is written to a hardcoded Feishu app token and table name, and the full record content is logged.\n[SQP-2] expected: Confirmed in SKILL.md and README: Feishu app credentials are required, which fits the purpose, but the docs omit basic guidance that FEISHU_APP_SECRET is sensitive.\n[SC1] expected: Confirmed in package.json: dotenv and node-fetch use caret dependency ranges. This is a low-level supply-chain/reproducibility issue and is partly mitigated by the included package-lock.json.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789068751510}}}}}